   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Consider the curve (x - y)^2 = 4x, for which dy/dx = (x - y - 2)/(x - y). The horizontal line y = k is tangent to the curve. What is the value of k?"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Negate",
         1
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "A horizontal tangent needs the numerator to vanish: x - y - 2 = 0, so y = x - 2.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Subtract",
            "x",
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Substitute y = x - 2 into the curve: (x - (x - 2))^2 = 4 = 4x, so x = 1.",
         "mathjson": 1
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Then y = 1 - 2 = -1, and the denominator x - y = 1 - (-1) = 2 is nonzero, so the tangent at (1, -1) is horizontal and k = -1.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Negate",
            1
         ]
      }
   ],
